index 0000000..7d87b2d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/PICASSO-KERNEL-NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# picasso (SM7250) kernel adaptation
+
+This patch set carries the SM7250-specific build-side additions that the pinned
+upstream UniXNU tree does not provide for picasso. It is applied on top of the
+upstream revision pinned by upstream.rev by the ./unixnu wrapper.
+
+## Contents
+
+- patches/xnu/offline-component-load-probes.patch: guards the
+  native_legacy_display_probe() call with XNU_NATIVE_LEGACY_DISPLAY. That probes
+  patch calls the symbol unconditionally under DEVELOPMENT||DEBUG, but the
+  definition only lives in the NativeLegacyDisplay archive, which the
+  first-console configuration does not link. bsd_init.o is compiled with
+  -DXNU_NATIVE_LEGACY_DISPLAY=${XNU_NATIVE_LEGACY_DISPLAY:-0} by
+  scripts/build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh, so with the option off the call disappears
+  and the kernel links; with it on the archive supplies the symbol. This
+  replaces the earlier no-op stub in bsd_init.c, which would collide with the
+  archive's definition once legacy display is enabled.
+- scripts/unixnu/kernel.py: when CONFIG_XNU_CRYPTO_BOOTSTRAP="source" the
+  prelink step copies the freshly built Mach-O instead of prelinking against the
+  proprietary IPSW kernelcache. Only the source-only bring-up milestone
+  (configs/picasso_platform_defconfig) selects that mode; the default
+  picasso_defconfig uses "prelinked" and keeps the upstream path.
+
+The archive builder (scripts/build-arm-driver.py) and the DriverKit header
+restore (scripts/prepare-xnu-source.py) are real files of this device
+repository, not injected by this patch. The unixnu driver copies a device
+repository's scripts/ into the build tree, so they replace upstream's copies of
+the same name.
+
+## Stage
+
+First-console bring-up: corecrypto (upstream builder), ArmDTPlatform and ArmCpu
+archives, architectural timer, PAN, DT panic region and the trust cache
+runtime. UFS / VirtIO / display / Adreno archives join the [kernel] archives
+list of board.toml in later stages.
